# Grades module (P9) — demo requests (VS / Rider / VS Code REST Client).
#
# One-time local setup (Development) is the same as users.http.
# Prerequisites: scheduling.http + lifecycle.http (active term, a group the professor teaches, registered students).
# Workflow (decision D3): professor drafts → Student Affairs confirms the group → Student Affairs publishes the term.

@host = http://localhost:5080
@adminToken = paste-the-admin-token-here
@professorToken = paste-the-teaching-professors-token-here
@studentToken = paste-a-registered-students-token-here
@termId = paste-the-active-term-id-here
@groupId = paste-a-group-id-here
@studentId = paste-a-roster-students-id-here
@gradeId = paste-a-grade-id-from-the-group-view-here

### Teacher or Student Affairs: the group's roster with each student's grade (null until drafted)
GET {{host}}/api/grades/groups/{{groupId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{professorToken}}

### Teacher: draft scores (0–100, 2 decimals); letters come from the subject faculty's scale.
### Roster students only, each once (400 entries[i].studentId); confirmed/published rows → 409.
PUT {{host}}/api/grades/groups/{{groupId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{professorToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "entries": [ { "studentId": "{{studentId}}", "score": 87.5 } ] }

### Student Affairs: confirm the group (every roster student needs a grade, else 400 listing missingStudentIds)
POST {{host}}/api/admin/grades/confirm
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "groupId": "{{groupId}}" }

### Student Affairs: publish the term's confirmed grades (optionally subjectId / groupId) → { published: n }; students are notified
POST {{host}}/api/admin/grades/publish
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "termId": "{{termId}}" }

### Student: published grades per term with term GPA and cumulative GPA (optional ?termId=)
GET {{host}}/api/grades/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### Student Affairs: correct a published grade (reason required; drafts/confirmed → 409); the student is notified
POST {{host}}/api/admin/grades/{{gradeId}}/correct
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "score": 91, "reason": "Exam re-marked after an addition error." }

### Student Affairs: the grade's correction history
GET {{host}}/api/admin/grades/{{gradeId}}/corrections
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
